  "verbalization": "Beractant is implicated in the pathogenesis of Newborn Respiratory Distress Syndrome through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Beractant is associated with Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS), which in turn is linked to other agents such as Poractant Alfa, Colfosceril Palmitate, and Lucinactant. These agents are all indicated to treat ARDS, and their association with Newborn Respiratory Distress Syndrome implies a potential role in the management of this condition. The shared indication of ARDS across these entities suggests a common mechanism of action or therapeutic effect, possibly involving the modulation of inflammatory responses or surfactant dysfunction. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Beractant in the treatment of ARDS, which may extend to the management of newborn respiratory distress syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
